<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Elmet</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 617 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small British kingdom around Leeds that held out against the Angles until Edwin of Northumbria expelled its king Ceretic around 617.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Elmet emerged after Roman rule ended as a British kingdom in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-yorkshire">West Yorkshire</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennines">Pennines</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vale-of-york">Vale of York</a>. It is remembered in place names such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sherburn-in-elmet">Sherburn-in-Elmet</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barwick-in-elmet">Barwick-in-Elmet</a>, and a 6th-century memorial stone at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llanaelhaearn">Llanaelhaearn</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Gwynedd</a> names a man of Elmet.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Very little is known of its government. Welsh poetry praises a king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwallawg-ap-lleenog">Gwallawg</a>, possibly of Elmet, who fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urien-rheged">Urien of Rheged</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a>. The kingdom survived surrounded by the growing Anglian powers of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-deira">Deira</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a>, perhaps protected by its wooded and marshy terrain and by dyke systems such as those near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barwick-in-elmet">Barwick</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/historia-brittonum">Historia Brittonum</a> records that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria">Edwin of Northumbria</a> seized Elmet and expelled its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceretic-of-elmet">Ceretic</a>, usually dated around 617. The district appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tribal-hidage">Tribal Hidage</a> as the Elmetsæte, and its people were absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-northumbria">Northumbria</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-elmet.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Elmet" width="320" height="383"><figcaption>Image: myself · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yr.Hen.Ogledd.550.650.Koch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 617 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gwallawg, Ceretic</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Elmet</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=534&amp;focus=kingdom-of-elmet" aria-label="Kingdom of Elmet on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4655 329 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Elmet lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4975 585L4945 553"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4945 553h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4975 585h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4975 585h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=534&amp;focus=kingdom-of-elmet">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

